  "conclusions": [
    "No normal TX expiry, driver short-write or driver error increment in the dual-link query window; loss is before USB driver admission.",
    "UsbSink droppedPackets combines scientific DATA and both compact/ADS diagnostic packet calls. +511 must not be called +511 scientific-frame drops.",
    "Serial sinkDropped +659 and lineDropped +149 localize the losses to admission; differing query windows account for the one-count difference from UsbSink +511.",
    "The real old source permits priority-7 AsyncLog to enqueue science, two summary packets and diagnostic lines into one four-record FIFO before priority-4 serialTx can run. Production host reproduction rejects the next science record with timeout/partial counters unchanged.",
    "Observed diagnostic adjacency supports the burst mechanism but raw RX alone cannot reconstruct scheduler timing of a rejected packet.",
    "The same firmware USB-only control captures 10913 frames without a sequence gap per root analyzer and usbDrop delta0; native USB bandwidth is not established as the dual-link bottleneck.",
    "New class-specific dataRejected/logRejected make the next HIL evidence distinguish science admission from diagnostic refusal."
